  "content": {
    "id": "p51-q29-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "29",
    "prompt": "A fruit grower accidentally made a 5% strength chemical mixture to spray his grape vines.\nThe strength of spray should be 8%.\nHe then adds pure chemical until the strength reaches 8%. The final volume is 350 litres.\nHow much pure chemical did he have to add?\nRound your answer to 2 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$11.05\\text{ L}$",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the volume of pure chemical added (L), and $y$ be the initial volume of 5% mixture (L).\n$$\\begin{align*}x+y&=350 &&(1)\\\\x+0.05y&=0.08(350)\\\\x+0.05y&=28 &&(2)\\end{align*}$$\n$(2)-0.05\\times(1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x+0.05y-0.05(x+y)&=28-0.05(350)\\\\0.95x&=10.5\\\\x&=\\frac{210}{19}\\\\x&\\approx11.05\\text{ L}\\end{align*}$$\nHe adds 11.05 litres of pure chemical, to 2 decimal places.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
